The value axis
description: the self-value's types - JSON Schema's set, binary added, its own subtyping
- 'The self-value''s type keeps JSON Schema''s set. It is not flat - it subtypes:'
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: bullets>
  - '`null` - the **singleton**: its only value is null (`~`, or a bare `a:`). A type that is also a value.'
  - '`boolean` · `number` · `integer` - with `integer` a subtype of `number` (a number whose value is whole).'
  - '`string` - refined by `format` (`text/markdown`, `text/x-latex`, ...); a bare string''s default prose format is `text/marklower`.'
  - '`binary` - the yamlover addition: opaque bytes, refined by `format` (`image/png`, `application/pdf`, `int32/le`). YAML''s `!!binary` (base64) is the same value.'
  - '`scalar` - the alias for "any leaf value": a value facet allowing every type above.'
- >
  `format` is **not a type** - it refines a facet, usually the value facet, and has an open
  sub-lattice of its own (whether `text/markdown` subtypes `text/plain` is deliberately unsettled).
  Closed `scalar` - a leaf with no fields - and the *open* value facet differ exactly on omni nodes:
  the open reading includes a scalar that has grown entries.
- 'YAML''s extra collection "types" are refinements of the facets, not new corners:'
- !!<format: text/plain> |
  binary     → {value: {type: binary, format: image/png},
                keyed: false, ordinal: false}    # value axis
  timestamp  → {value: {type: string, format: date-time},
                keyed: false, ordinal: false}    # value axis
  set        → {value: false,
                ordinal: {uniqueItems: true}}    # a dedup FLAG
  omap       → {value: false, ordinal: false}    # = object - maps are
                                                 #   ALREADY ordered
  pairs      → {value: false, keyed: false,      # ordered [k, v]s;
                ordinal: {items: ...}}             #   keys may repeat
- >
  A facet carries a small fixed set of modifier keywords beyond false-or-schema - `uniqueItems` (set),
  key-uniqueness (omap versus pairs), ordering (yamlover's default) - almost all kept verbatim from
  JSON Schema. The merge key `<<` and YAML's `!!value` are mechanisms, not types.
